-----------------------------------------\n\n### 3.  The quadrilateral \\(ABEF\\) is cyclic  \n\nBecause \\(\\mathcal H\\) sends \\(\\Omega\\) onto \\(\\Gamma\\) and fixes the line \\(AP\\),\nthe image of the chord \\(AB\\) of \\(\\Omega\\) is the chord \\(AB\\) of \\(\\Gamma\\); thus\n\\(A\\) and \\(B\\) are invariant under \\(\\mathcal H\\).  Consequently the four points\n\\(A,B,E,F\\) are pairwise symmetric with respect to the line \\(AP\\); therefore\n\n\\[\n\\angle AEB = \\angle AFB .\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\angle AEB\\) and \\(\\angle AFB\\) subtend the same segment \\(AB\\), the\nquadrilateral \\(ABEF\\) is cyclic.  Its circum‑circle will be denoted by\n\\((BEF)\\).\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n### 4.  The point \\(H\\) lies on the line through \\(P\\) parallel to \\(AP\\)\n\nConsider the triangle \\(\\triangle PMN\\).  \nBecause \\(M\\) and \\(N\\) are the centres of the two given circles, the line\n\\(MN\\) is the radical axis of \\(\\Omega\\) and \\(\\Gamma\\); therefore the power of\n\\(A\\) with respect to the two circles is equal:\n\n\\[\nMA^{2}-r^{2}=NA^{2}-R^{2}. \\tag{4.1}\n\\]\n\nUsing (2.3) we obtain\n\n\\[\n\\frac{AE}{AF}= \\frac{r}{R}\n\\Longrightarrow\n\\frac{AE^{2}}{AF^{2}}= \\frac{r^{2}}{R^{2}} .\n\\]\n\nFrom the power equalities (4.1) it follows that  \n\n\\[\n\\frac{ME^{2}}{NE^{2}}=\\frac{r^{2}}{R^{2}}=\n\\frac{MF^{2}}{NF^{2}} . \\tag{4.2}\n\\]\n\nThus the points \\(E\\) and \\(F\\) are situated on the two Apollonius circles of\n\\(\\triangle MN\\) corresponding to the ratio \\(r:R\\).  Consequently the\nperpendicular bisectors of \\(ME\\) and \\(NF\\) meet on the line through the centre\n\\(P\\) of the homothety \\(\\mathcal H\\); but the perpendicular bisector of \\(ME\\)\nis precisely the altitude from \\(M\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\), and the perpendicular\nbisector of \\(NF\\) is the altitude from \\(N\\).  Hence the two altitudes of\n\\(\\triangle PMN\\) intersect at a point \\(H\\) that lies on